    {
      "id": 33268,
      "name": "TheJayMann",
      "username": "TheJayMann",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/thejaymann/{size}/2261_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-10-07T21:05:05.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>That brings up an interesting thought. Without thinking about it, I would simply agree with what most everyone said, that with Darken the Skies already played, the mask would not trigger it's effect.&nbsp; However, to remain consistant with this, when the Mask is already in play, it's effect would have to trigger before the text on the just played card is read, another set of fowl cards plus one nonfowl card would be played, and, if applicable, the last nonfowl card played would have it's results before the first nonfowl card played, not counting event effects, although, based on memory alone, she has a&nbsp;small amount of one-shot cards, so the latter situation isn't too likely.</p>",
      "post_number": 7,
      "post_type": 1,
